.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt DF 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm df
.Nd report shared filesystem space and session mount access
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Print one filesystem's data capacity, used and available space in
1024-byte units, rounded-up percentage used, and commit sequence.
The filesystem id identifies that backing filesystem.
Used space includes blocks held by the committed image or accepted changes;
reserved metadata regions are outside the reported data-block count.
.Pp
Then print this session's mount paths in sorted order and their read-only
or read-write access.
These are views of the same filesystem, not separate Unix filesystems.
All sessions share the same free space; there are no per-session quotas.
The commit column is an observation, not a commit request.
.Pp
There are no operands or options: even
.Ql --
and
.Fl Fl help
are usage errors.
The command requires this process's active file-server channel.
A direct block handle does not substitute for it.
An absent channel, a channel lent to a running child, or file-server refusal
is reported on standard error.
No data or mount authority is changed.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 for a successful report; 1 for a file-server request failure;
2 if any argument is supplied.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
df
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr stat 1 ,
.Xr sync 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7 ,
.Xr handles 7
